      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_size",
      "narration": "It's a muscle about the size of a fist, split into four chambers: two atria on top and two ventricles below.",
      "on_screen_text": "Four chambers",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Four"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_two",
      "narration": "It's really two pumps: the right side sends blood to the lungs, and the left side to the rest of the body.",
      "on_screen_text": "Two pumps in one",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Two"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_lungs",
      "narration": "Oxygen-poor blood goes to the lungs, picks up oxygen and comes back to the heart.",
      "on_screen_text": "Oxygen from the lungs",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Oxygen"
      ],
      "sfx": "bubbles",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_body",
      "narration": "And the left ventricle, the strongest one, pushes it all around the body.",
      "on_screen_text": "The strongest one",
      "highlight_words": [
        "strongest"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_spark",
      "narration": "Every beat starts with an electrical spark in the sinus node: your natural pacemaker.",
      "on_screen_text": "An electrical spark",
      "highlight_words": [
        "spark"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_squeeze",
      "narration": "That signal makes the atria squeeze first and, an instant later, the ventricles.",
      "on_screen_text": "Top first, then bottom",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Top",
        "bottom"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cor_valves",
      "narration": "And the thump-thump you hear is the valves snapping shut so blood can't flow backward.",
      "on_screen_text": "Thump-thump = valves",
      "highlight_words": [
        "valves"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
