  "description": "The heart is a fist-sized muscle with four chambers. The right side sends blood to the lungs and the left side to the rest of the body. Each beat starts with an electrical signal from the sinus node; the atria contract, then the ventricles, and the 'thump-thump' is the valves closing. It beats about 100,000 times and pumps about 7,000 liters a day. Simplified original 3D animation; not medical advice.",
